Optimization with Scattering Project: 
Consider M number of objects in space, each with a sound hard boundary conditions. I.e. u(n) = 0; du/dn = 0. We have originally designed / written codde that woudl solve the field u(x,y) at any given point for a incoming field (via a scattering matrix formulation + GMRES). 
Now consider the optimization problem where there are M number of objects in space, and there are n number of points along the boundary of the space ( in theory they could be anywhere), and we want to maximize the magnitude of the field at this points, w.r.t. different input parameters of the system such as rotational angle, shape of elipse etc. (further descirbed in the system). 


The project will be broken up into phases / with descriptions and corresponding code files: 
1. Phase one: Implments scattering matrix for the problem with quadrature weights correction, solves with accurancy up to eps and implments scattering matrix with rotation of arbitrary angle 
files: 
kress_weights, S_kess, D_kress, N_kress, T_diff_kress -- implmenetaion of quadrature correction weights 
scattering_matrix_full -- scattering matrix via BIE 
scattering_An_arb -- single row of scattering matrix 
Rotate-scattering_matrix -- implements scattering matrix with rotation of a certain angle 

2: Phase two: implments function that solves the field via output from scattering matrix (betas) 
files: 
building_translation_matrix -- budils M2L matrices (objects to objects scattering matrix) 
Buiild_insident_coefficeint -- translates incoming field to coefficeint alphas 
solve_multiple_scattering -- sovles for coeffcient beta 
eval_field_ms -- evaluates fields from beta 

3. Phase tree: implements FMM on the scattering matrix to speed it up 
files: 
fmm_box_assign -- box partitioning 
fmm_params -- select FMM parameters 
fmm_min_box_size -- pick min box size 
fmm_aggregation -- aggregation matrices 
fmm_translation_plane_wave 
fmm_near matrix 
fmm_precompute 
fmm_matvec
solve_multiple_scattering_fmm -- FMM-GMRES solver 

4. Phase four: compute field on a full grid instead of one point 
files: 
compute_field_grid 

5. Phase five: builds the experiments 
1) builds experiment set up for rotational angle 
files: 
build_H_matrix 
compute_objective 
solve_adjoint
compute_gradient_rotation 




